{
  "title": "A turn that ends while the client is away",
  "description": "Sections 8, 9, 10 and 12. The phone leaves while the agent waits for permission. The laptop attaches, answers from the pending list with host/answer, and watches the turn end. When the phone loads the session again it gets the whole record and then the turn's ended notice.",
  "steps": [
    {"note": "Open a connection to the host (through its relay, or on the LAN).", "conn": "phone", "connect": "host"},
    {"note": "The first frame is host/hello: the versions this client speaks and the device credential from pairing.", "conn": "phone", "send": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "method": "host/hello", "params": {"protocol": {"min": "0.1", "max": "0.1"}, "client": {"name": "oal-conformance", "version": "0.1.0"}, "auth": {"type": "device", "deviceId": "{{deviceId}}", "token": "{{token}}"}}}},
    {"note": "The host picks 0.1 and says which device this connection is. `info` is the same object host/info returns.", "conn": "phone", "expect": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"protocol": "0.1", "device": {"id": "{{deviceId}}"}, "info": {"host": {"id": "{{hostId}}"}}}}},
    {"note": "ACP starts every agent channel with initialize. The host answers it itself with the agent's capabilities; the client's are not passed on.", "conn": "phone", "send": {"agent": "{{agent}}", "acp": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "method": "initialize", "params": {"protocolVersion": 1, "clientCapabilities": {"fs": {"readTextFile": false, "writeTextFile": false}, "terminal": false}, "clientInfo": {"name": "oal-conformance", "version": "0.1.0"}}}}},
    {"note": "ACP protocol version 1. No sign-in methods: the agent runs under its owner's own sign-in on the host.", "conn": "phone", "expect": {"agent": "{{agent}}", "acp": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"protocolVersion": 1, "agentCapabilities": {"loadSession": true}, "authMethods": []}}}},
    {"note": "ACP session/new, unchanged. cwd is the agent's folder from host/agents; a remote client can't pick another folder or add MCP servers that run commands.", "conn": "phone", "send": {"agent": "{{agent}}", "acp": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "method": "session/new", "params": {"cwd": "{{folder}}", "mcpServers": []}}}},
    {"note": "The agent's own session id and modes. This connection is now attached to the session.", "conn": "phone", "expect": {"agent": "{{agent}}", "acp": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"sessionId": "{{session}}", "modes": {"currentModeId": "ask", "availableModes": [{"id": "ask"}, {"id": "folder"}, {"id": "full"}]}}}}},
    {"note": "The phone sends a prompt that needs permission.", "conn": "phone", "send": {"agent": "{{agent}}", "acp": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 3, "method": "session/prompt", "params": {"sessionId": "{{session}}", "prompt": [{"type": "text", "text": "run: echo hi"}]}}}},
    {"note": "The turn starts.", "conn": "phone", "expect": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "host/turn", "params": {"agent": "{{agent}}", "sessionId": "{{session}}", "turnId": "{{turn}}", "state": "running"}}},
    {"note": "The tool call.", "conn": "phone", "expect": {"agent": "{{agent}}", "acp": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "session/update", "params": {"sessionId": "{{session}}", "update": {"sessionUpdate": "tool_call", "toolCallId": "{{call}}", "title": "echo hi", "kind": "execute", "status": "pending"}}}}},
    {"note": "The permission request.", "conn": "phone", "expect": {"agent": "{{agent}}", "acp": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": "{{phoneReq}}", "method": "session/request_permission", "params": {"sessionId": "{{session}}", "toolCall": {"toolCallId": "{{call}}", "title": "echo hi"}, "options": [{"optionId": "allow-once", "kind": "allow_once"}, {"optionId": "reject-once", "kind": "reject_once"}]}}}},
    {"note": "The phone goes away before answering.", "conn": "phone", "close": true},
    {"note": "Open a connection to the host (through its relay, or on the LAN).", "conn": "laptop", "connect": "host"},
    {"note": "The first frame is host/hello: the versions this client speaks and the device credential from pairing.", "conn": "laptop", "send": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "method": "host/hello", "params": {"protocol": {"min": "0.1", "max": "0.1"}, "client": {"name": "oal-conformance", "version": "0.1.0"}, "auth": {"type": "device", "deviceId": "{{deviceId}}", "token": "{{token}}"}}}},
    {"note": "The host picks 0.1 and says which device this connection is. `info` is the same object host/info returns.", "conn": "laptop", "expect": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"protocol": "0.1", "device": {"id": "{{deviceId}}"}, "info": {"host": {"id": "{{hostId}}"}}}}},
    {"note": "ACP starts every agent channel with initialize. The host answers it itself with the agent's capabilities; the client's are not passed on.", "conn": "laptop", "send": {"agent": "{{agent}}", "acp": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "method": "initialize", "params": {"protocolVersion": 1, "clientCapabilities": {"fs": {"readTextFile": false, "writeTextFile": false}, "terminal": false}, "clientInfo": {"name": "oal-conformance", "version": "0.1.0"}}}}},
    {"note": "ACP protocol version 1. No sign-in methods: the agent runs under its owner's own sign-in on the host.", "conn": "laptop", "expect": {"agent": "{{agent}}", "acp": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"protocolVersion": 1, "agentCapabilities": {"loadSession": true}, "authMethods": []}}}},
    {"note": "The laptop attaches to the session.", "conn": "laptop", "send": {"agent": "{{agent}}", "acp": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "method": "session/load", "params": {"sessionId": "{{session}}", "cwd": "{{folder}}", "mcpServers": []}}}},
    {"note": "The record: the prompt...", "conn": "laptop", "expect": {"agent": "{{agent}}", "acp": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "session/update", "params": {"sessionId": "{{session}}", "update": {"sessionUpdate": "user_message_chunk", "content": {"type": "text", "text": "run: echo hi"}}}}}},
    {"note": "...and the tool call so far.", "conn": "laptop", "expect": {"agent": "{{agent}}", "acp": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "session/update", "params": {"sessionId": "{{session}}", "update": {"sessionUpdate": "tool_call", "toolCallId": "{{call}}", "title": "echo hi", "kind": "execute", "status": "pending"}}}}},
    {"note": "A turn is running.", "conn": "laptop", "expect": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "host/turn", "params": {"agent": "{{agent}}", "sessionId": "{{session}}", "turnId": "{{turn}}", "state": "running"}}},
    {"note": "Attached.", "conn": "laptop", "expect": {"agent": "{{agent}}", "acp": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"modes": {"currentModeId": "ask"}}}}},
    {"note": "The pending request, as a copy for this connection.", "conn": "laptop", "expect": {"agent": "{{agent}}", "acp": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": "{{laptopReq}}", "method": "session/request_permission", "params": {"sessionId": "{{session}}", "toolCall": {"toolCallId": "{{call}}", "title": "echo hi"}, "options": [{"optionId": "allow-once", "kind": "allow_once"}, {"optionId": "reject-once", "kind": "reject_once"}]}}}},
    {"note": "The laptop looks at the pending list, as an inbox would.", "conn": "laptop", "send": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 3, "method": "host/pending", "params": {}}},
    {"note": "The request is there, with its host-wide id.", "conn": "laptop", "expect": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 3, "result": {"requests": [{"id": "{{pending}}", "agent": "{{agent}}", "sessionId": "{{session}}", "toolCall": {"toolCallId": "{{call}}"}}]}}},
    {"note": "It answers from the list with host/answer rather than on the agent channel.", "conn": "laptop", "send": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 4, "method": "host/answer", "params": {"id": "{{pending}}", "optionId": "allow-once"}}},
    {"note": "Accepted.", "conn": "laptop", "expect": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 4, "result": {}}},
    {"note": "Its own copy of the ACP request is withdrawn, since every copy is.", "conn": "laptop", "expect": {"agent": "{{agent}}", "acp": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "$/cancel_request", "params": {"requestId": "{{laptopReq}}"}}}},
    {"note": "Answered with -32800.", "conn": "laptop", "send": {"agent": "{{agent}}", "acp": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": "{{laptopReq}}", "error": {"code": -32800, "message": "Request cancelled"}}}},
    {"note": "Resolved, by this device.", "conn": "laptop", "expect": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "host/pending_update", "params": {"change": "resolved", "request": {"id": "{{pending}}"}, "outcome": {"outcome": "selected", "optionId": "allow-once"}, "answeredBy": {"deviceId": "{{deviceId}}"}}}},
    {"note": "The result.", "conn": "laptop", "expect": {"agent": "{{agent}}", "acp": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "session/update", "params": {"sessionId": "{{session}}", "update": {"sessionUpdate": "tool_call_update", "toolCallId": "{{call}}", "status": "completed", "content": [{"type": "content", "content": {"type": "text", "text": "hi"}}]}}}}},
    {"note": "The reply.", "conn": "laptop", "expect": {"agent": "{{agent}}", "acp": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "session/update", "params": {"sessionId": "{{session}}", "update": {"sessionUpdate": "agent_message_chunk", "content": {"type": "text", "text": "Done."}}}}}},
    {"note": "The turn ends while the phone is away.", "conn": "laptop", "ordered": true, "expect": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "host/turn", "params": {"agent": "{{agent}}", "sessionId": "{{session}}", "turnId": "{{turn}}", "state": "ended", "stopReason": "end_turn", "usage": {"inputTokens": 12, "outputTokens": 5, "totalTokens": 17}}}},
    {"note": "The phone comes back.", "conn": "phone", "connect": "host"},
    {"note": "host/hello.", "conn": "phone", "send": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "method": "host/hello", "params": {"protocol": {"min": "0.1", "max": "0.1"}, "client": {"name": "oal-conformance", "version": "0.1.0"}, "auth": {"type": "device", "deviceId": "{{deviceId}}", "token": "{{token}}"}}}},
    {"note": "Authenticated.", "conn": "phone", "expect": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"protocol": "0.1", "device": {"id": "{{deviceId}}"}}}},
    {"note": "ACP starts every agent channel with initialize. The host answers it itself with the agent's capabilities; the client's are not passed on.", "conn": "phone", "send": {"agent": "{{agent}}", "acp": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "method": "initialize", "params": {"protocolVersion": 1, "clientCapabilities": {"fs": {"readTextFile": false, "writeTextFile": false}, "terminal": false}, "clientInfo": {"name": "oal-conformance", "version": "0.1.0"}}}}},
    {"note": "ACP protocol version 1. No sign-in methods: the agent runs under its owner's own sign-in on the host.", "conn": "phone", "expect": {"agent": "{{agent}}", "acp": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"protocolVersion": 1, "agentCapabilities": {"loadSession": true}, "authMethods": []}}}},
    {"note": "It loads the session.", "conn": "phone", "send": {"agent": "{{agent}}", "acp": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "method": "session/load", "params": {"sessionId": "{{session}}", "cwd": "{{folder}}", "mcpServers": []}}}},
    {"note": "The record: the prompt,", "conn": "phone", "expect": {"agent": "{{agent}}", "acp": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "session/update", "params": {"sessionId": "{{session}}", "update": {"sessionUpdate": "user_message_chunk", "content": {"type": "text", "text": "run: echo hi"}}}}}},
    {"note": "the tool call,", "conn": "phone", "expect": {"agent": "{{agent}}", "acp": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "session/update", "params": {"sessionId": "{{session}}", "update": {"sessionUpdate": "tool_call", "toolCallId": "{{call}}", "title": "echo hi", "kind": "execute", "status": "pending"}}}}},
    {"note": "its result,", "conn": "phone", "expect": {"agent": "{{agent}}", "acp": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "session/update", "params": {"sessionId": "{{session}}", "update": {"sessionUpdate": "tool_call_update", "toolCallId": "{{call}}", "status": "completed", "content": [{"type": "content", "content": {"type": "text", "text": "hi"}}]}}}}},
    {"note": "and the reply.", "conn": "phone", "expect": {"agent": "{{agent}}", "acp": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "session/update", "params": {"sessionId": "{{session}}", "update": {"sessionUpdate": "agent_message_chunk", "content": {"type": "text", "text": "Done."}}}}}},
    {"note": "Then the most recent host/turn: the ended notice of the turn that finished while it was away, with its outcome and usage. It comes after the record.", "conn": "phone", "ordered": true, "expect": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "host/turn", "params": {"agent": "{{agent}}", "sessionId": "{{session}}", "turnId": "{{turn}}", "state": "ended", "stopReason": "end_turn", "usage": {"inputTokens": 12, "outputTokens": 5, "totalTokens": 17}}}},
    {"note": "The load answer. No permission request follows: nothing is pending.", "conn": "phone", "expect": {"agent": "{{agent}}", "acp": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"modes": {"currentModeId": "ask"}}}}}
  ]
}
